this is Kareem Davina speaking on the  behalf of Jean Luc psyche  what could a resonable for remake look  like that's the question on a lot of  fans minds after the report that Capcom  is planning on remaking resident before  the idea has left the internet a little  divided change on the one hand resonable  four is many people's personal favorite  and the prospect of it being lovingly  recreated in the beautiful ari engine  actually sounds pretty red I'll buy it  at a high price but for others resin  evil 4 is the pinnacle of the series and  as a result doesn't need to be remade  for any reason outside of it potentially  making a buttload of money no thanks  this is how I felt at first but the more  I think about it the more I realize how  boring would be to just remaster it with  no changes after all the RA 1 remake in  the RA to remake are two of my favorite  games so Capcom has proven that you can  make something great even better  so let's come up with some ideas for how  a game already as great as a Resident  Evil 4 could be even better ok for  starters  even though resin evil 4 is so beloved  there's actually one aspect that is  absolutely universally disliked hey take  it easy  no one likes Ashley well I didn't mind  her she does what I tell her to do and  she's very good at it  but she's a rather simple companion and  we've had a lot of excellent AI partners  and video games in the year since  lovable characters with complex  narratives and useful mechanics that  make you want them around Ashley well is  none of those things granted she's  helpless by design an objective you need  to protect but her complete lack of  self-preservation instinct feels archaic  and at its worst frustrates players  trying to keep her safe which leaves a  great opportunity to improve her in a  remake now I don't think you need to  give Ashley a gun but as an extra set of  eyes she could provide alerts to players  of incoming enemy ambushes she could  also inform Leon of nearby treasure or  maybe scavenge the loot enemies drop she  could even have an inventory slot that  can hold a single item of your choice  such as a spare health spray  which she can use on Liana in a tricky  situation by giving her small but  helpful things to do she could become  much less of a nuisance now when I think  of my favorite moments from Resident  Evil 4 I recall a terrifying opening  village sequence the first El Gigante  fights when you're assisted by an  adorable pup and the unexpected shift to  a gothic castle run by this guy I've  been expecting you basically my fondest  memories all come from the first half of  the game and rarely the second half  that's not to say that the second half  is bad I just don't think is a strong in  particular chapter 4 feels like the  weakest part of the game as the pacing  slows down quite a bit at this point in  the game I'm ready to fight Salazar and  escape the castle but oops ashley is  kidnapped a gun and Leia needs to trek  through the mine and make his way back  up there are great sequences in this  chapter like the minecart chase and 4 do  go but I can sort of take or leave the  rest dripping down chapter 4 could solve  this but I think there is potential in  moving these sections to after the  Salazar fight to help pacing or even  reworking them entirely there's a lot of  opportunity to improve this part of the  game and even out the pacing while  punching up set pieces to make it feel  as memorable as the earlier half playing  resin evil 4 for the first time back in  2007 yes it was the Wii version and yes  it's still one of the best versions of  the game don't at me I was surprised by  how often a game threw me off guard whoa  whoa whoa whoa you're throwing a  one-hit-kill chainsaw guy I mean the  first five minutes of the game wait  you're telling me if I shoot them in the  head instead of killing them they could  get even more [ __ ] up the dog comes  back and helps you oh my god this is the  greatest game ever made moments like  these felt special and memorable and  unfortunately they won't hit nearly the  same and a remake because I've already  experienced them which is why I'd love  it if the remake didn't adhere 100% of  the original and mix things up to create  new moments what if the chainsaw guy  didn't show in the opening but instead  is somewhere completely unexpected or  they had new enemy types that are  somehow even more terrifying than a  plague of busting  of a dudes head I'm not saying they need  to change everything but throw in enough  new surprises to help create new  memories for returning players a perfect  example of this would be the QuickTime  events for the record I think cuties are  a huge part of the identity of resonable  4 and I would like to see them stay in a  remake at their best they keep the  player on their toes with the potential  for one to happen at any moment if you  succeed you feel like a pro gamer and if  you mess up you get a ridiculous death  that's good for a laugh it's an element  of surprise that makes the QuickTime  events so good which is why it's emitted  ly easy to become bored of them on  repeat playthroughs of the game  so for remake what if they kept  QuickTime events but completely changed  when and how they happen this could all  be introduced via a remix mode that  changes up the variables for repeat  playthroughs if capcom wants to really  stay true to the original in the main  campaign last thing I want to touch on  is something that's near and dear to my  heart and that's the voice acting I sent  my right hand to be smaller than you  your right hand comes off because more  so than any other Resident Evil  I think resonable forest voice acting is  a key component to the game I think that  many lines in the game are even more  iconic than Jill sandwich curse everyone  going bingo for as annoying as Ashley  can be the specific way she yells will  forever be ingrained into my brain 4  also has the best version of Leon s  Kennedy or as my girlfriend called him  daddy Herbert he manages to be  simultaneously the coolest and dorkiest  video game protagonist with some  absolute cheeseball one-liners hasta  luego trying to recapture the magic of  old voice recording is next to  impossible Metal Gear Solid Twin Snakes  is an excellent example of that snake  hey you're that ninja if the other  resident evil' remakes are any  indication Capcom will probably want to  make enough changes to the script that  reusing these old recordings won't be  possible  heck they probably won't get the same  voice actors back Paul Mercier Leon's  voice actor in for hasn't done a voice  role since 2014 which is why I think  they should not even bother trying to  replicate that original magic and go  their own path with it I still want a  cheesy I want Salazar hamming it up and  Leone making lame jokes but if it was  just the same line for line I would be  constantly comparing it to the original  imagine that is an incredibly tall order  and I'm sure I'll still won't be fully  satisfied just because of how ingrained  in my brain rising before his dialogue  is but I do believe this would be the  best way to go about it except for the  merchant those are some of the best  videogame lines ever recorded and should  not be touched in any way is that old  stranger is that old stranger is that  old stranger is that old thank you I  could go on forever about all the small  things they could tweak like letting me  switch guns without opening the menu and  how they need to keep the fort in front  of the logo even though it makes a no  sense but I wanted to stick to broader  elements that I really care about so it  turned to you all in the comments to let  me know what you'd like to see in a  resident for remake and don't just say  nothing it's perfect come on I know  there's got to be something you want to  see improved and if you like this video  and my ideas let me know and if you did  like them you can also let me know sorry  to have bothered you I look forward to  returning to this video in several years  and seeing if any of this actually  panned out thanks for watching  [Music]

